  "question": {
    "text": "Number of solutions of <math><msup><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mo>(</mo><mo>|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>|</mo><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow><mrow><mo>|</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">c</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">o</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>|</mo></mrow></msup></math> in <math> <mrow> <mrow><mo>[</mo> <mrow> <mo>−</mo><mi>π</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>π</mi></mrow> <mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></math>, is equal to",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "4",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>In the interval <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\" separators=\"|\"><mrow><mo>–</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">π</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&nbsp;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">π</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> all the values of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>sin</mi><mo>|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>|</mo></math> are positive as well as <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>|</mo><mi>cos</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>|</mo></math><br />Hence in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\" separators=\"|\"><mrow><mo>–</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">π</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&nbsp;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">π</mi></mrow></mfenced></math>, equation gets reduced to,&nbsp;</p><p><math><msup><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">sin</mi></mrow><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">cos</mi></mrow><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></msup></math><br />Taking log on both sides,<br /><math><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">sin</mi></mrow><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">log</mi></mrow><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">cos</mi></mrow><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">log</mi></mrow><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></mrow></math><br /><math><mo>⇒</mo><mi>&nbsp;</mi><mfenced close=\"|\" open=\"|\" separators=\"|\"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">tan</mi></mrow><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">log</mi></mrow><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">log</mi></mrow><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></math> , value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>tan</mi><mi>x</mi></math> are positive in <math><msup><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></mrow></msup></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mn>3</mn><mrow><mi>r</mi><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup></math> quadrant and negative in <math><msup><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup></math> and <math><msup><mrow><mn>4</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mi>h</mi></mrow></msup></math> quadrant but positive for <math><mfenced close=\"|\" open=\"|\" separators=\"|\"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">tan</mi></mrow><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfenced></math> in all the values of <math><mi>x</mi></math> in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\" separators=\"|\"><mrow><mo>–</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">π</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&nbsp;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">π</mi></mrow></mfenced></math>.</p><p>Hence, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>tan</mi><mi>x</mi></math> will repeat its value in all <math><mn>4</mn></math> quadrants, so the number of solutions are <math><mn>4</mn></math> .</p>",
    "image": null
  },
